  "explanation": "After a thorough review of the original RTL source code and the candidate patches, no concrete mechanism can be established linking any candidate edit to the observed failure on `o_sck` (cycles 101–110). The public trace shows `o_sck` stuck high during the first SPI transaction after startup, yet the candidate patches all insert unrelated gating conditions into the low-level startup counter logic or the command/response state machine. Those gating changes do not alter the core SCK-generation path (`o_sclk`/`o_sck`) that is driven by `r_state`, `r_z_counter`, and `r_clk_counter` in `llsdspi`. Since the failure is a cycle-exact port mismatch on the SPI clock itself and none of the candidates touch the clock-generation or state-transition logic responsible for that port, there is no evidence-based basis to rank any candidate above another. The checklist therefore remains empty."
}
